\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The main window displays the checkboxes in four logical rows, as one compact block to the right of Performance Mode and Max Workers. Each checkbox indicator aligns with the top text line of its label. The first-column sequence etreeDB, setlist.fm, setlist.fm upgrade, and Thorough Setlist Matching now uses the same compact vertical row spacing all the way down; the wrapped Tag Copy/Delete Original label no longer makes the third row taller and push Thorough farther down. Thorough Setlist Matching and Tag Copy/Delete Original still use two-line labels, with their second lines extending downward. Checkbox widget and row padding remain minimized without overlap, while the logical four-row/four-column assignments are unchanged. The boxed Corruption Handling group now runs as one single horizontal strip directly beneath the performance/checkbox options: Corrupt files followed immediately by its drop-down, Folder removal followed immediately by its drop-down, then Folder corruption threshold followed immediately by the compact value box and % sign. The threshold control is disabled unless Folder removal is At threshold. No default corruption summary is shown below the group; validation errors still appear. At startup, TLO measures the requested main-window size before showing it and clamps the initial geometry when necessary so the first visible window remains within the current screen with room for normal window borders and a taskbar or dock. When Thorough Setlist Matching is selected with neither etreeDB nor setlist.fm enabled, no Thorough-specific Info line is shown. If an online lookup source is enabled, the Thorough Info line simply names the enabled source or sources; the normal setlist.fm limit warning still appears when applicable. Row 1, left to right: etreeDB, Compliant, Tag in Place, Artist in Album Tag. Row 2: setlist.fm, Rename Compliantly, Tag Copy, Convert shn. Row 3: setlist.fm upgrade, As-Is Artist Name, Tag Copy/Delete Original, Dry run. Row 4 begins with Thorough Setlist Matching; the remaining cells are unused. Thorough Setlist Matching defaults off. The setlist.fm upgrade checkbox is directly beneath setlist.fm and has effect only while setlist.fm is enabled. Compliant and Rename Compliantly are mutually exclusive: checking either one automatically unchecks the other.}
